      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "## Topology Observability Overview\nThis dashboard summarizes the current live topology slice exposed by the platform. It focuses on bounded, real evidence: topology node and link counts, state distributions, inference-boundedness, endpoint-pairing depth, node-participation depth, collection posture, backend-versus-collector agreement, persisted sync-history freshness, serving-mode posture, and delivery coverage posture for the topology read side.\n\nCurrent limits:\n- The topology model is live and useful, but intentionally partial.\n- Links are inferred from interface naming and operational state rather than LLDP, IGP, or ODL enrichment.\n- Comparison panels here show aggregate delivery and agreement posture, not protocol-derived drift truth.\n- Partiality is now read through four bounded cues: inference posture, endpoint-pairing posture, node-participation posture, and collection posture.\n- Evidence-posture panels show source, freshness, and bounded-confidence labels only; they do not turn Grafana into topology validation logic.\n- Partial knowledge remains explicit through degraded links, single-sided links, isolated nodes, blocked or degraded collection labels, backend-ready coverage ratios, and partial sync-history results.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "title": "Dashboard Scope",
      "type": "text"
    },
